===persian===

شاید این بلبل که می‌خواند منم
آن یکی شاید
که بوی یاس‌ها را دوست می‌دارد.
من همهٔ خود نیستم
قسمتی از ابر شاید
چند برگ از شاخهٔ گردو.
خط‌خطی‌هایی درون ماه می‌بینم
که روزی در نگاه دختری هم بود،
هر دو لحنی مثل یک آواز را دارند
مثل یک آواز ناخوانده.
خط‌خطی‌ها را
سعی خواهم کرد
میهمان حنجرم باشند،
بخشی از مهتاب یک شب
قسمتی از ابر روزی
میهمانِ حنجر مَحزون سیما بود.
شاید این بلبل که می‌خواند
آن یکی شاید
که بوی یاس‌ها را دوست می‌دارد
من نباشم
دیگری باشد
دوستی با نام اصغر
که همیشه در سکوتش حالِ خواندن داشت...
رفت یک شب
جای دیگر حالِ ماندن داشت.
رفت یک شب
مثل برگ از شاخهٔ گردو
رفت یک شب
مثل عطر
از خاطرِ شب بو
۱۳۷۲/۶/۳

===machine===

Perhaps this nightingale that is singing is me,
or perhaps that other one,
the one who loves the smell of the jasmines.
I am not all of myself —
part cloud, perhaps,
a few leaves off the walnut branch.
I see scribblings inside the moon
that were once in a girl's eyes as well;
both carry a tone like one same song,
like one song never sung.
The scribblings —
I will try
to make them guests of my throat;
a share of one night's moonlight,
a part of some day's cloud,
was the guest of Sima's mournful throat.
Perhaps this nightingale that is singing,
or perhaps that other one,
the one who loves the smell of the jasmines,
is not me —
is someone else,
a friend by the name of Asghar,
who always, in his silence, had a singing in him...
He went, one night —
Somewhere else, he had a staying in him.
He went, one night,
like a leaf off the walnut branch;
he went, one night,
like scent
out of the memory of the night-stock.
1372/6/3

===lantern===

Perhaps this nightingale that is singing is me,
or perhaps it is the other one,
the one who loves the smell of the jasmines.
I am not all of myself —
part cloud, perhaps,
a few leaves off the walnut branch.
I see scribblings inside the moon
that were once in a girl's eyes as well;
both carry a tone like one same song,
like one song never sung.
The scribblings — I will try
to make them guests of my throat;
a share of one night's moonlight,
a part of some day's cloud,
was once the guest of Sima's mournful throat.
Perhaps this nightingale that is singing,
or perhaps that other one,
the one who loves the smell of the jasmines,
is not me at all —
is someone else,
a friend by the name of Asghar,
who always had a singing in his silence...
He went, one night.
Somewhere else, he had a staying in him.
He went, one night,
like a leaf off the walnut branch.
He went, one night,
like scent out of the memory of the night-stock.

1372/6/3

===translation===

===footnotes===

An elegy that spends twenty lines refusing to say who it is about. The nightingale might
be the poet, might be someone else; only at the end does the someone else get a name, and by then
he has already gone.

سیما is either a woman's name or the ordinary word for a face. The line will carry both and the
printed text does not choose.
